<title>INDIA: India 1996 tea output seen at 780 mln kg v 750 mln.</title>
<headline>India 1996 tea output seen at 780 mln kg v 750 mln.</headline>
<dateline>COONOOR, India 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's state-run Tea Board said on Monday it estimated a record 1996 production of 780 million kgs against 750 million in 1995.</p>
<p>India's previous record high was 757 million kgs in 1993.</p>
<p>Planters said the record crop this year is expected mainly due to fair weather conditions especially in the north.</p>
<p>The Tea Board said the northern regions would contribute 594 million kgs with the remaining 186 million contributed by the south. In 1995, the north contributed 568 million kgs and the south 182 million.</p>
</text>
